# Allowlist: nothing enters the build context unless it's named at the bottom. What the Dockerfile
# build actually reads:
#
#   package.json, package-lock.json   `npm ci` (both stages) and the runtime image
#   vite.config.ts                    `npm run build`: TanStack Start, Nitro and Tailwind setup
#   tsconfig.json                     the "@/..." import alias (vite-tsconfig-paths)
#   src/                              the app itself, including routeTree.gen.ts, styles.css, and
#                                     src/server/sse-node.ts and start-queue-worker.ts, which
#                                     vite.config.ts points Nitro at
#
# Everything else stays out, on purpose:
#   - .env and every other secret: docker-compose passes .env to the running app (env_file)
#   - node_modules, .output, .tanstack, .nitro, .vercel: installed or built fresh inside the image
#   - .git, .claude, .gstack/, .superpowers/, docs/, scratch/
#   - one-off root scripts (script*.ts, verify-mailcow.ts, fix-sogo.ts, clear-queue.ts, diag-batch.ts)
#   - files the build never reads: drizzle.config.ts, migrations/, drizzle/, supabase/, api/,
#     scripts/, inngest/, components.json (shadcn CLI only), eslint/prettier/vitest configs
#
# There's no public/ folder today. If one is added for static files, allow it here: !public
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!src
